d 'USEPACKAGE': module to find, verify, and install the user-written packages (and data) a do-file needs
d
d  usepackage takes the list of user-written packages a do-file
d needs and makes sure they are installed, so a shared do-file can
d open with one line instead of a stack of ssc install / net
d install commands or a paragraph telling the reader to go run
d findit. For each name it checks whether it is already installed,
d then SSC, then the net search catalogue (which covers the Stata
d Journal and the STB), reporting what it found, what it skipped,
d and why. The name you ask for is often a COMMAND rather than a
d PACKAGE -- dropmiss ships inside dm89_2, bacon inside st0197.
d usepackage resolves that case, but because the mapping is
d inferred it asks before installing, and in a batch run it
d declines rather than guessing (see noconfirm). Ancillary files (a
d package's example do-files and datasets, which net install does
d not place on the adopath) are fetched by default and reported;
d noancillary skips them. github() installs a package straight from
d a GitHub repository, probing branch (main, then master) and the
d usual layouts for stata.toc; give it a bare owner and it searches
d that account's repositories by name, or set the global
d usepackage_github once and any unresolved name is looked for
d there. It uses only raw.githubusercontent.com for installs, so it
d is not rate-limited the way the GitHub code-search API is. data()
d fetches data files out of a GitHub repository, guessing the live
d branch and transparently resolving Git LFS pointers, which the
d raw endpoint otherwise serves as a 130-byte text stub that Stata
d cannot read. scan() reads a do-file and reports which of its
d commands do not resolve on this machine. usepackage does not
d check versions; pair it with require (Correia and Seay, Stata
d Journal 24(4)) when you need minimum or exact versions pinned.
d Version 1.0.0 (2011) was written at the Public Policy Research
d Institute, Texas A&M University. 
d
d KW: user-written packages; findit; search; ssc install; net install; ancillary files; github; git lfs; reproducibility
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.0
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f ../e/example_usepackage.do
f usepackage.ado
f usepackage.sthlp
